# Test: ze config fmt -w - is a pipeline stage. It writes the formatted config
# to standard output, always, even when the input needed no change.
#
# VALIDATES: a stdin-only OUTPUT route is reachable from a .ci. With a real
#   path, `-w` rewrites the file in place, prints "Formatted: <path>" on stderr
#   and writes nothing when the input already agrees with the serializer. With
#   "-" it emits the config on stdout every time (cmdFmt,
#   internal/component/config/cli/cmd_fmt.go).
# PREVENTS: the branch being unreachable. The runner replaced the verb's own "-"
#   with a file path until 2026-09-07, so this ran the in-place arm against a
#   file and no .ci could assert the pipeline arm at all.
#
# Every stream assertion is FILE-level, over the concatenated output of both
# commands (docs/architecture/testing/ci-format.md). So each needle here is
# unique to the command it sits under: seq=1 carries 127.0.0.1 and 1.2.3.4,
# seq=2 carries 127.0.0.2 and 5.6.7.8. Each command asserts its own exit code
# with exit=, because expect=exit:code= reaches only the last one.
#
# Discrimination, one assertion per property of the branch:
#   seq=1 pipes a mis-indented config whose `remote { ip ... }` block the
#     serializer collapses to one `remote ip ...` line. That line is in no
#     input, so the assertion fails against a command that echoes stdin.
#   seq=2 pipes a config that is ALREADY formatted, so `hasChanges` is false.
#     The in-place arm writes nothing at all in that case.
#   the reject names the note the in-place arm prints for the changed input of
#     seq=1, which a pipeline stage never emits.
#   Delete the `cliio.IsStdin(configPath)` arm of cmdFmt, so the in-place arm
#   runs, and the seq=2 assertion and the reject both go red.

stdin=unformatted:terminator=EOF_UNFORMATTED
bgp {
peer peer1 {
connection {
remote {
ip 127.0.0.1
}
}

session {
asn {
local 65000
remote 65001
}
router-id 1.2.3.4
}
}
}
EOF_UNFORMATTED

stdin=formatted:terminator=EOF_FORMATTED
bgp {
	peer peer2 {
		connection {
			remote ip 127.0.0.2
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65010
				remote 65011
			}
			router-id 5.6.7.8
		}
	}
}
EOF_FORMATTED

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config fmt -w -:stdin=unformatted:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=remote ip 127.0.0.1

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config fmt -w -:stdin=formatted:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=router-id 5.6.7.8

reject=stderr:contains=Formatted
